💡 **SUGGESTION: Doc duplication — link instead of restating**

Lines 7-21 restate, near-verbatim, the paint-path explanation that already lives on `frameContentLines` in `pty_harness.dart:39-51` (and a third condensed variant was just added to `job_board_stability_pty_test.dart:300-303`).

Three copies of a subtle renderer explanation will drift: the next reader who learns a new detail (e.g. another paint path, or a fix in `vendor/dart_tui`) must update all of them. Since the unit test imports `pty_harness.dart` anyway, consider keeping the full narrative in one place (the harness doc) and reducing this header to the test-specific contract, e.g.:

```dart
/// Unit proof for the gh-982 flake diagnosis: raw viewport equality also
/// compares xterm buffer-cell materialization, not content — see
/// [frameContentLines] in pty_harness.dart for the paint-path mechanics.
/// These tests pin, deterministically and without spawning a PTY:
/// ... (keep the three test intents)
```

No CI risk either way (the jscpd dup gate scans `lib/` only) — pure maintainability.

